<title>USA: N.Y.S. baord says tables for now LIPA bond vote.</title>
<headline>N.Y.S. baord says tables for now LIPA bond vote.</headline>
<dateline>ALBANY, N.Y. 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York State Public Authorities Control Board said Wednesday questions spurred it to table for now a vote on whether to approve a bonding plan to finance the takeover of the Long Island Lighting Co. by the Long Island Power Authortiy (LIPA).</p>
<p>The proposed $7.3 billion tax-exempt bond financed takeover of LILCO was approved by the board of trustees of LIPA on Monday. However, questions about the LIPA plan delayed the control board's vote, a spokesman for the board said Wednesday.</p>
